1
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:46,048
After all of my matches were finally over, I got horribly sick with a fever.

2
00:01:46,048 --> 00:01:51,388
I spent December 31st alone in my dimly lit room.

3
00:01:52,388 --> 00:01:54,808
I don't know if I've ever been that sick before.

4
00:02:01,508 --> 00:02:12,188
Thirsty. So thirsty. Water.

5
00:02:12,188 --> 00:02:30,108
I have to... I have to eat something.

6
00:02:30,868 --> 00:02:33,888
I gotta take more medicine.

7
00:02:35,168 --> 00:02:37,308
But there's only one pill left.

8
00:02:37,308 --> 00:02:45,668
I need to buy more. But how? I can't... do anything.

9
00:02:52,128 --> 00:02:59,948
I'll forget it. I'll just... go back to sleep. A deep sleep.

10
00:02:59,948 --> 00:03:07,308
Maybe when I wake up, my fever will be gone. As if it was all a bad dream.

11
00:03:08,888 --> 00:03:11,848
I stayed in the apartment alone for days.

12
00:03:11,848 --> 00:03:20,208
I was burning up with a fever.

13
00:03:20,908 --> 00:03:23,128
Having the same dream over and over again.

14
00:03:23,748 --> 00:03:25,948
It's been that way ever since I was a kid.

15
00:03:26,928 --> 00:03:29,728
The same dream haunting me again and again.

16
00:03:32,728 --> 00:03:36,088
I find myself going up a never-ending escalator.

17
00:03:36,088 --> 00:03:39,628
It's not like it's really scary or anything.

18
00:03:40,628 --> 00:03:42,528
I just keep going up.

19
00:03:43,088 --> 00:03:44,168
Higher and higher.

20
00:03:44,848 --> 00:03:47,088
And when I finally reach the top...

21
00:03:47,088 --> 00:03:53,188
There's no way to get back down.

22
00:04:06,088 --> 00:04:07,508
Who is it?

23
00:04:08,068 --> 00:04:08,988
Who's there?

24
00:04:09,948 --> 00:04:11,308
It's too loud.

25
00:04:15,628 --> 00:04:18,188
Stop it. Knock it off.

26
00:04:19,188 --> 00:04:21,608
I can't get up.

27
00:04:25,648 --> 00:04:28,128
Ray! Ray!

28
00:04:30,528 --> 00:04:32,008
Ray! Ray!

29
00:04:33,208 --> 00:04:35,248
Momo's here. Why?

30
00:04:35,248 --> 00:04:36,488
Ray! Ray!

31
00:04:39,928 --> 00:04:40,408
Why?

32
00:04:45,288 --> 00:04:47,788
As I expected. I knew you had a cold.

33
00:04:48,048 --> 00:04:49,128
All right, guys. Go!

34
00:04:49,308 --> 00:04:49,608
Roger!

35
00:04:50,328 --> 00:04:50,768
Yay!

36
00:04:51,288 --> 00:04:52,068
It's Ray!

37
00:04:52,288 --> 00:04:53,548
Hina, secure the pillow.

38
00:04:53,668 --> 00:04:53,988
Roger!

39
00:04:54,228 --> 00:04:56,348
Ray, grab your phone, wallet, and keys.

40
00:04:57,728 --> 00:04:59,668
Stay in your PJs and put on a jacket.

41
00:05:01,528 --> 00:05:03,248
Let's wrap this scarf around your neck.

42
00:05:03,488 --> 00:05:04,808
There's a taxi waiting outside.

43
00:05:04,808 --> 00:05:06,208
Ah, a taxi.

44
00:05:06,628 --> 00:05:07,348
But why?

45
00:05:07,508 --> 00:05:08,468
Where are we going?

46
00:05:08,908 --> 00:05:09,908
What do you mean where?

47
00:05:10,648 --> 00:05:12,828
We're taking you to the doctor right now.

48
00:05:13,248 --> 00:05:16,448
If you have the flu, you'll be quarantined and we'll take care of you here.

49
00:05:16,828 --> 00:05:18,048
But if it's just a cold...

50
00:05:18,048 --> 00:05:20,668
We're taking you to our house.

51
00:05:24,748 --> 00:05:25,768
Here you go.

52
00:05:25,768 --> 00:05:29,588
Thank goodness it wasn't the flu.

53
00:05:29,588 --> 00:05:33,928
We have to be very careful not to let Grandpa or Momo get exposed.

54
00:05:36,368 --> 00:05:37,868
The egg porridge is ready.

55
00:05:38,208 --> 00:05:39,068
Try and have some.

56
00:05:39,588 --> 00:05:42,468
I saw your kitchen, Ray, and you haven't been eating much.

57
00:05:42,468 --> 00:05:45,468
Do you like pickled plums?

58
00:05:45,948 --> 00:05:46,828
Here, have one.

59
00:05:47,828 --> 00:05:51,268
It can help to make you feel better, especially when you have a fever.

60
00:05:51,588 --> 00:05:52,468
Hold still a sec.

61
00:05:52,848 --> 00:05:53,728
Lift up your chin.

62
00:05:53,968 --> 00:05:54,248
Good.

63
00:05:55,388 --> 00:05:57,068
Keep this towel around your neck.

64
00:05:57,288 --> 00:05:58,648
I'll change it if it gets sweaty.

65
00:05:59,308 --> 00:06:00,868
The porridge will heat you up a lot.

66
00:06:01,368 --> 00:06:03,108
Sweating it out will help reduce your fever.

67
00:06:03,108 --> 00:06:06,748
We've got plenty of towels, so no problem there.

68
00:06:08,688 --> 00:06:09,168
Sorry.

69
00:06:09,588 --> 00:06:11,968
I just need to wipe off your forehead a bit.

70
00:06:13,308 --> 00:06:14,508
Momo, now!

71
00:06:16,348 --> 00:06:17,788
I'll bet you now!

72
00:06:18,468 --> 00:06:20,088
Um, thank you for the meal.

73
00:06:20,288 --> 00:06:21,028
That's yummy!

74
00:06:21,268 --> 00:06:22,508
Momo wants a two!

75
00:06:22,648 --> 00:06:24,428
No, Momo, this is only for Ray.

76
00:06:27,988 --> 00:06:30,008
All right, you ate quite a bit.

77
00:06:30,168 --> 00:06:30,908
That's great.

78
00:06:30,908 --> 00:06:33,808
Why don't you have some tea and go lie down?

79
00:06:34,728 --> 00:06:38,528
But before that, don't you think we should call your family?

80
00:06:38,948 --> 00:06:40,568
They must be worried about you.

81
00:06:41,028 --> 00:06:44,728
Yeah, but I live on my own now, so we don't have to call.

82
00:06:45,348 --> 00:06:45,788
Tenderines!

83
00:06:45,848 --> 00:06:47,388
Kitties don't like citrus!

84
00:06:47,548 --> 00:06:49,148
Yummy tenderines!

85
00:06:49,988 --> 00:06:50,508
Hmm.

86
00:06:52,408 --> 00:06:53,908
On your own, huh?

87
00:06:54,468 --> 00:06:55,988
Let me see your phone for a minute.

88
00:06:57,328 --> 00:06:59,608
Hasn't your battery been dead for a few days?

89
00:07:00,908 --> 00:07:14,708
You can't say you're alone with all these messages.

90
00:07:15,168 --> 00:07:16,688
People are worried about you.

91
00:07:17,628 --> 00:07:18,188
You see?

92
00:07:18,188 --> 00:07:22,888
Yeah.

93
00:07:29,888 --> 00:07:30,568
Hello?

94
00:07:31,248 --> 00:07:34,248
Um, hi, Father.

95
00:07:34,788 --> 00:07:35,608
It's Ray.

96
00:07:36,268 --> 00:07:38,048
Ray, is that you?

97
00:07:38,448 --> 00:07:39,448
Are you all right?

98
00:07:39,988 --> 00:07:40,728
What's wrong?

99
00:07:40,948 --> 00:07:41,748
Do you have a cold?

100
00:07:41,748 --> 00:07:45,588
You weren't answering your phone, so I was gonna stop by your place.

101
00:07:46,008 --> 00:07:47,248
Are you sure you're okay?

102
00:07:48,808 --> 00:07:51,488
The moment I heard my father's voice on the phone,

103
00:07:51,928 --> 00:07:55,068
I realized just how selfish I'd been.

104
00:07:56,928 --> 00:08:01,048
From his voice, I could tell that he was really worried about me.

105
00:08:01,048 --> 00:08:04,548
What an idiot.

106
00:08:05,308 --> 00:08:07,968
All this time, I had only been thinking about myself.

107
00:08:09,008 --> 00:08:12,488
But, I hadn't even thought about those around me.

108
00:08:17,428 --> 00:08:17,948
Ray?

109
00:08:18,368 --> 00:08:19,448
How are you doing?

110
00:08:20,888 --> 00:08:22,008
Feel like getting up?

111
00:08:22,588 --> 00:08:24,288
You should have some food and medicine.

112
00:08:24,288 --> 00:08:30,148
I just knew it.

113
00:08:30,268 --> 00:08:32,308
Can you wake me up right before midnight?

114
00:08:32,908 --> 00:08:35,308
Let me know when New Year's breakfast is ready.

115
00:08:35,608 --> 00:08:38,648
Try not to wake me up until it's time to eat.

116
00:08:40,248 --> 00:08:43,148
I just knew this would happen, as usual.

117
00:08:44,048 --> 00:08:45,788
It used to be even worse.

118
00:08:46,148 --> 00:08:49,468
We had three more people back then and it was pretty cramped.

119
00:08:50,528 --> 00:08:52,668
There wasn't even enough room to breathe.

120
00:08:52,668 --> 00:08:55,728
Three people.

121
00:08:56,588 --> 00:08:58,068
Oh, I see.

122
00:08:58,648 --> 00:08:59,828
Their father too.

123
00:09:00,768 --> 00:09:03,628
Every year, me, mom, and grandma were the last ones up.

124
00:09:04,148 --> 00:09:06,708
Everyone else would fall asleep and we'd be left with the dishes.

125
00:09:07,328 --> 00:09:10,788
That's how we always saw the old year go out and the new year come in.

126
00:09:13,508 --> 00:09:15,728
Something serious must have happened here.

127
00:09:17,108 --> 00:09:18,908
But no one talks about it.

128
00:09:19,468 --> 00:09:21,228
They never mention their father.

129
00:09:21,228 --> 00:09:23,508
The tour will begin in June.

130
00:09:23,728 --> 00:09:24,988
Here, have some.

131
00:09:25,568 --> 00:09:26,688
Don't you feel hungry?

132
00:09:27,288 --> 00:09:29,388
I didn't want to wake you, but you should eat.

133
00:09:30,048 --> 00:09:30,628
Oh, really?

134
00:09:31,068 --> 00:09:32,628
Have some pickled plums too.

135
00:09:33,128 --> 00:09:37,648
I think it'll still be refreshing for you even though you can't taste very much right now.

136
00:09:38,288 --> 00:09:39,348
Um, wait.

137
00:09:39,928 --> 00:09:41,168
Didn't I say that earlier?

138
00:09:41,168 --> 00:09:45,608
Whenever I was sick, that's what my mom used to say to me.

139
00:09:46,388 --> 00:09:49,588
And here I am, saying the same thing she said.

140
00:09:50,168 --> 00:09:54,008
Whenever she'd bring up the pickled plums, I'd think, there she goes again.

141
00:09:54,528 --> 00:09:56,088
But it was always comforting.

142
00:09:57,148 --> 00:10:00,068
Mom's words always made me feel better, like magic.

143
00:10:00,068 --> 00:10:06,168
But she was gone before Momo had a chance to know that.

144
00:10:06,848 --> 00:10:07,608
Poor thing.

145
00:10:11,408 --> 00:10:14,948
I, um, can't thank you enough for all you've done.

146
00:10:15,828 --> 00:10:17,148
I don't know what I'd do without you.

147
00:10:17,648 --> 00:10:21,968
On such an important day like New Year's Eve, you brought me here and took care of me,

148
00:10:22,388 --> 00:10:24,188
even though I'm not really part of your family.

149
00:10:24,188 --> 00:10:26,068
No, you're wrong.

150
00:10:26,288 --> 00:10:27,848
I wanted you to be here.

151
00:10:30,188 --> 00:10:31,848
You're the one who helped me.

152
00:10:33,428 --> 00:10:35,088
If you weren't here right now,

153
00:10:35,648 --> 00:10:39,468
the truth is I'd probably be cleaning up by myself and crying.

154
00:10:40,108 --> 00:10:43,448
So I can't thank you enough for being here with us.

155
00:10:48,808 --> 00:10:49,568
Hey, wait.

156
00:10:49,708 --> 00:10:50,488
What's wrong, Rei?

157
00:10:50,668 --> 00:10:51,728
Why are you crying?

158
00:10:51,728 --> 00:10:54,428
Oh no, you'll make me cry.

159
00:10:55,648 --> 00:10:59,388
As we sat there together, drying our eyes and sniffling,

160
00:10:59,888 --> 00:11:02,628
we could hear the New Year's Eve bells ringing on TV.

161
00:11:05,328 --> 00:11:09,608
Another sad year coming to an end, vanishing into the night.

162
00:11:10,808 --> 00:11:13,428
I had been so distracted by my own loneliness

163
00:11:13,428 --> 00:11:16,988
that I had failed to see it in the others around me.

164
00:11:17,668 --> 00:11:19,288
It was a sad realization.

165
00:11:19,288 --> 00:11:22,028
The New Year's Eve bells rang in my heart,

166
00:11:22,708 --> 00:11:23,828
filling me with emotion.

167
00:11:24,548 --> 00:11:27,088
Just like a wide river softly flowing,

168
00:11:27,708 --> 00:11:29,068
the New Year had begun,

169
00:11:29,648 --> 00:11:31,788
moving slowly on its way.

170
00:11:31,788 --> 00:11:45,808
What on earth?

171
00:11:46,368 --> 00:11:48,928
Which one of you put stickers on my drawers?

172
00:11:50,048 --> 00:11:51,048
I'm sorry.

173
00:11:53,328 --> 00:11:55,908
Do you know how hard it is to peel this off?

174
00:11:55,908 --> 00:11:57,248
I'm sorry.

175
00:11:57,248 --> 00:11:57,328
I'm sorry.

176
00:11:57,328 --> 00:11:57,528
I'm sorry.

177
00:12:04,528 --> 00:12:05,328
Mom and...

178
00:12:05,328 --> 00:12:07,328
Chihiro.

179
00:12:09,068 --> 00:12:09,968
A dream?

180
00:12:11,868 --> 00:12:12,648
Hey, Rei.

181
00:12:13,268 --> 00:12:14,068
Good morning.

182
00:12:14,368 --> 00:12:14,948
Hi, Rei.

183
00:12:15,028 --> 00:12:15,788
How do you feel?

184
00:12:16,068 --> 00:12:17,968
Akari says it's time for us to have breakfast.

185
00:12:18,548 --> 00:12:19,588
I'll be right there.

186
00:12:20,048 --> 00:12:20,788
How's your fever?

187
00:12:21,128 --> 00:12:22,288
I think it's gone down.

188
00:12:22,888 --> 00:12:23,988
I should be fine now.

189
00:12:26,668 --> 00:12:28,108
Hey, good morning, everyone.

190
00:12:28,748 --> 00:12:29,428
Good morning.

191
00:12:29,868 --> 00:12:31,068
Happy New Year, Rei.

192
00:12:31,588 --> 00:12:33,068
Hey, Happy New Year.

193
00:12:35,748 --> 00:12:38,148
There are so many ads in the paper today.

194
00:12:38,208 --> 00:12:38,888
Packed!

195
00:12:42,028 --> 00:12:43,488
What are you doing, Momo?

196
00:12:43,728 --> 00:12:44,788
I'm reading the paper.

197
00:12:45,408 --> 00:12:46,968
Would you like some mochi, Rei?

198
00:12:47,388 --> 00:12:48,128
What's happening?

199
00:12:48,428 --> 00:12:49,868
I'll have sweet soy sauce.

200
00:12:50,228 --> 00:12:51,148
Cheese for Momo.

201
00:12:51,148 --> 00:12:53,688
Uh, then I'll have cheese, too.

202
00:12:54,608 --> 00:12:55,788
Then let's move on.

203
00:12:55,888 --> 00:12:56,848
Please, go ahead.

204
00:12:57,148 --> 00:12:57,968
Hello there.

205
00:12:58,148 --> 00:12:59,248
Happy New Year.

206
00:12:59,468 --> 00:13:00,668
How are you all doing this morning?

207
00:13:00,668 --> 00:13:01,908
You still have a fever.

208
00:13:03,108 --> 00:13:04,928
Well, let's get some food in you.

209
00:13:05,288 --> 00:13:06,228
Then take your medicine.

210
00:13:07,228 --> 00:13:08,168
Get under the kotatsu.

211
00:13:09,028 --> 00:13:10,728
You can warm your feet under here.

212
00:13:15,528 --> 00:13:17,888
I think the mailman's here.

213
00:13:17,888 --> 00:13:22,008
I've got the New Year's pose eyes!

214
00:13:22,328 --> 00:13:23,188
This one's for me.

215
00:13:23,308 --> 00:13:24,128
That's for Akari.

216
00:13:24,688 --> 00:13:25,508
One for me.

217
00:13:25,768 --> 00:13:26,468
Another one.

218
00:13:26,788 --> 00:13:27,268
Akari.

219
00:13:27,628 --> 00:13:28,728
And that's for Ampah's.

220
00:13:28,928 --> 00:13:30,148
Here's one for you, Momo.

221
00:13:30,388 --> 00:13:30,908
For me?

222
00:13:31,168 --> 00:13:31,528
What?

223
00:13:31,948 --> 00:13:32,388
What?

224
00:13:32,528 --> 00:13:33,268
What is it?

225
00:13:33,308 --> 00:13:34,408
Yeah, what's that?

226
00:13:35,128 --> 00:13:35,608
So?

227
00:13:35,828 --> 00:13:36,628
Are there a lot?

228
00:13:36,948 --> 00:13:37,308
Yeah.

229
00:13:37,668 --> 00:13:39,428
I think we got more than last year.

230
00:13:39,728 --> 00:13:40,188
Wow.

231
00:13:40,448 --> 00:13:41,328
And Momo, too?

232
00:13:41,748 --> 00:13:42,688
How exciting.

233
00:13:42,988 --> 00:13:43,348
Uh-huh.

234
00:13:44,068 --> 00:13:44,868
Oh, yeah.

235
00:13:45,128 --> 00:13:46,128
You might have some, right?

236
00:13:46,288 --> 00:13:47,008
At your place.

237
00:13:47,108 --> 00:13:47,728
Oh, huh.

238
00:13:47,888 --> 00:13:48,628
At my place?

239
00:13:48,748 --> 00:13:49,488
I don't think so.

240
00:13:51,448 --> 00:13:52,328
Oh, go get him!

241
00:13:52,708 --> 00:13:53,608
You stay right here.

242
00:13:53,688 --> 00:13:54,348
I won't be lost.

243
00:13:54,368 --> 00:13:55,148
I just need to borrow your shoes.

244
00:13:55,148 --> 00:13:55,168
Hold on.

245
00:13:55,168 --> 00:13:57,308
Then you'll find out how pathetic I really am.

246
00:14:00,468 --> 00:14:00,868
Hi.

247
00:14:01,168 --> 00:14:01,988
I'm back.

248
00:14:01,988 --> 00:14:09,168
So, um, you did get a few.

249
00:14:09,608 --> 00:14:10,468
Looks like two.

250
00:14:10,908 --> 00:14:11,948
Yeah, just two.

251
00:14:12,308 --> 00:14:12,708
What?

252
00:14:12,808 --> 00:14:13,508
I got some?

253
00:14:13,708 --> 00:14:15,028
I didn't think I'd get any.

254
00:14:15,868 --> 00:14:16,788
Who's this from?

255
00:14:17,928 --> 00:14:18,188
Ah!

256
00:14:18,388 --> 00:14:19,408
It's Badoo!

257
00:14:19,828 --> 00:14:21,188
He calls that a cottage?

258
00:14:21,488 --> 00:14:22,248
Looks like a palace!

259
00:14:22,548 --> 00:14:24,148
Wait, he's also got a hot air balloon?

260
00:14:24,568 --> 00:14:26,368
No, that can't really be his.

261
00:14:27,448 --> 00:14:28,948
So who's this one from?

262
00:14:28,948 --> 00:14:29,828
Ta-da!

263
00:14:30,868 --> 00:14:35,488
Tata-nori Jinguji, 16th Grandmaster Chairman of the Japan Shogi Association.

264
00:14:36,388 --> 00:14:36,868
Chairman?

265
00:14:37,708 --> 00:14:39,648
Um, what about Shogi?

266
00:14:39,908 --> 00:14:41,188
And with the sailfish?

267
00:14:41,268 --> 00:14:42,008
Who is that?

268
00:14:42,028 --> 00:14:42,548
Relation?

269
00:14:42,748 --> 00:14:44,288
I can't believe he went ahead with him.

270
00:14:44,928 --> 00:14:45,648
I'll say this.

271
00:14:45,688 --> 00:14:46,868
He was a strong player.

272
00:14:47,188 --> 00:14:48,908
Although he's always been a bit off.

273
00:14:49,188 --> 00:14:53,048
But even with this, keep in mind that he served as a Grandmaster for seven terms.

274
00:14:53,408 --> 00:14:55,088
Wait, why am I defending him?

275
00:14:55,088 --> 00:14:59,228
Hey, everybody!

276
00:15:00,108 --> 00:15:01,288
Happy New Year!

277
00:15:01,508 --> 00:15:03,108
Your Aunt Misaki's here!

278
00:15:03,548 --> 00:15:04,028
Done!

279
00:15:04,388 --> 00:15:06,828
Ah, it feels good to finally be home.

280
00:15:07,108 --> 00:15:10,428
Going to my husband's parents' house always makes my shoulders sore.

281
00:15:10,568 --> 00:15:11,008
Aunt Misaki!

282
00:15:11,008 --> 00:15:12,808
Now I can finally relax.

283
00:15:13,188 --> 00:15:14,788
That's because you're not yourself there.

284
00:15:14,908 --> 00:15:18,408
You've always cared a little too much about keeping up appearances.

285
00:15:18,408 --> 00:15:20,648
And you're pretty good at it, too.

286
00:15:21,208 --> 00:15:21,488
Oh!

287
00:15:23,068 --> 00:15:24,228
New Year's money!

288
00:15:24,548 --> 00:15:26,028
Hina, Momo, here you go!

289
00:15:27,608 --> 00:15:28,908
Thank you, Aunt Misaki!

290
00:15:29,128 --> 00:15:30,588
I can't wait to spend it!

291
00:15:30,608 --> 00:15:31,708
Thank you, Aunt Misaki!

292
00:15:31,808 --> 00:15:32,648
I like it!

293
00:15:33,068 --> 00:15:34,548
And for you, Dad!

294
00:15:35,088 --> 00:15:36,148
Oh, for me, too!

295
00:15:36,268 --> 00:15:36,928
Are you sure?

296
00:15:37,068 --> 00:15:38,088
This is for Akari!

297
00:15:38,348 --> 00:15:39,208
Really, Misaki?

298
00:15:39,448 --> 00:15:40,388
Thanks a lot!

299
00:15:40,788 --> 00:15:43,388
And here!

300
00:15:43,568 --> 00:15:46,608
For our very special guest, the Shogi Boy!

301
00:15:46,608 --> 00:15:48,108
Don't get too excited!

302
00:15:48,748 --> 00:15:52,188
Your Akari kidnapped you after you got a cold on New Year's Eve!

303
00:15:52,388 --> 00:15:53,028
Wait, what?

304
00:15:53,248 --> 00:15:53,828
But why?

305
00:15:54,168 --> 00:15:55,548
I can't take that from you!

306
00:15:56,348 --> 00:15:57,548
Of course you can!

307
00:15:57,808 --> 00:16:01,668
Not long ago, you brought Issa and Mr. Smith to my club, after all!

308
00:16:03,508 --> 00:16:05,508
I'll be counting on you to do it again!

309
00:16:08,728 --> 00:16:09,668
And finally...

310
00:16:09,668 --> 00:16:17,008
This is for you, Mom.

311
00:16:17,568 --> 00:16:20,108
Mikako, I came over for a visit.

312
00:16:24,508 --> 00:16:25,808
Happy New Year!

313
00:16:27,088 --> 00:16:28,908
Please bring us some more good luck.

314
00:16:28,908 --> 00:16:32,208
Hey, Misaki.

315
00:16:32,628 --> 00:16:34,808
Are you gonna make Akari work again this year?

316
00:16:35,168 --> 00:16:38,208
Stop using your relatives and just hire a new girl already.

317
00:16:38,688 --> 00:16:40,508
I never agreed to this, you know.

318
00:16:41,188 --> 00:16:43,548
I don't want Akari in dangerous situations.

319
00:16:43,928 --> 00:16:44,908
Just calm down.

320
00:16:45,448 --> 00:16:47,508
You know my club's not a dangerous place.

321
00:16:50,188 --> 00:16:52,208
It may be small, but it's refined.

322
00:16:52,208 --> 00:16:54,368
We mainly cater to regulars anyway.

323
00:16:54,848 --> 00:16:56,428
You know I treasure that club.

324
00:16:56,428 --> 00:16:58,528
Yeah, that's what you always say.

325
00:16:59,208 --> 00:17:04,388
Do you intend to keep Akari here doing all the housework and raising the kids until she's an old woman?

326
00:17:04,608 --> 00:17:05,808
She's an earnest girl.

327
00:17:06,028 --> 00:17:09,008
So she's committed to being a mother figure if she has to be.

328
00:17:09,148 --> 00:17:14,408
But she also needs to be pushed to put on makeup, wear a pretty outfit, and go out twice a week.

329
00:17:14,628 --> 00:17:16,368
She is a woman, after all.

330
00:17:17,068 --> 00:17:19,648
Even though she's a true beauty, what about her future?

331
00:17:19,988 --> 00:17:22,428
She may never marry if she's worn out by housework.

332
00:17:22,428 --> 00:17:27,548
Don't worry. I won't allow anyone to lay a finger on Akari at my club.

333
00:17:27,868 --> 00:17:31,528
No. Instead, I'll take their money without them ever touching her.

334
00:17:31,768 --> 00:17:33,468
You see, it's very delicate.

335
00:17:33,848 --> 00:17:36,588
If the clients can't touch her, they'll get all worked up.

336
00:17:36,708 --> 00:17:39,348
And then they'll start throwing money at the unattainable.

337
00:17:39,628 --> 00:17:41,928
While I make my move and grab it.

338
00:17:41,928 --> 00:17:45,308
Ah! Honey! Your daughter is a true demon!

339
00:17:45,728 --> 00:17:47,988
You gave birth to a hot-blooded demon!

340
00:17:48,428 --> 00:17:48,768
Ah!

341
00:17:52,088 --> 00:17:53,968
Are you going to be staying for dinner?

342
00:17:54,668 --> 00:17:57,748
Hina and I have been working hard to make everything just right.

343
00:17:57,968 --> 00:18:00,028
Sure. You don't have to twist my arm.

344
00:18:00,468 --> 00:18:02,308
Your uncle went to a soccer game anyway.

345
00:18:05,448 --> 00:18:06,508
Wow! Amazing!

346
00:18:06,748 --> 00:18:07,168
Ta-da!

347
00:18:07,168 --> 00:18:09,688
It took a lot of hard work to make all of that.

348
00:18:09,848 --> 00:18:12,168
And it all looks so modern. How nice!

349
00:18:12,668 --> 00:18:14,028
Hina and I came up with it.

350
00:18:14,028 --> 00:18:17,408
We put a lot of creative thought into each piece.

351
00:18:17,688 --> 00:18:20,728
But our goal was to make delicious, traditional New Year's food.

352
00:18:21,108 --> 00:18:23,868
It felt kind of boring to just cut fish cake into slices.

353
00:18:24,228 --> 00:18:29,028
So instead, we pounded the fish paste into balls and put them on skewers to look like cute little dumplings.

354
00:18:29,568 --> 00:18:32,288
You can't live a hearty life without pork and beans.

355
00:18:32,788 --> 00:18:36,428
For wealth, we made golden mashed sweet potatoes and chestnuts.

356
00:18:36,728 --> 00:18:40,508
Look through the holes in the lotus root and you can see a bright future ahead.

357
00:18:40,508 --> 00:18:44,808
Staying firmly rooted with the help of burdock root meat rolls.

358
00:18:45,668 --> 00:18:49,668
We pray that Grandpa lives long like turtles do, so mini hamburger turtles.

359
00:18:50,708 --> 00:18:54,268
And there's rolled omelet mixed with fish paste and sweet egg strips.

360
00:18:54,268 --> 00:18:57,968
Oops! I cut little hot dogs into the shape of cute tiny fish.

361
00:18:58,388 --> 00:18:58,808
See?

362
00:18:59,428 --> 00:19:01,148
Both of you are so incredible!

363
00:19:01,648 --> 00:19:05,408
Mikado and Grandmother used to make all the traditional New Year's dishes.

364
00:19:05,748 --> 00:19:07,388
I want biscotti and mine too!

365
00:19:07,648 --> 00:19:09,048
And gum, I want gum too!

366
00:19:09,048 --> 00:19:11,788
That's amazing New Year's food.

367
00:19:12,468 --> 00:19:14,008
Each dish is a different wish.

368
00:19:14,628 --> 00:19:20,668
When I look at this nest of empty boxes, it kind of makes me feel like I have to fill every one of them.

369
00:19:21,668 --> 00:19:25,928
And once we did, the final result was beyond rewarding!

370
00:19:26,728 --> 00:19:28,628
We knew the mission was accomplished!

371
00:19:29,048 --> 00:19:30,308
Cutest food ever!

372
00:19:30,788 --> 00:19:31,168
Yeah!

373
00:19:31,168 --> 00:19:32,768
Exactly!

374
00:19:33,388 --> 00:19:38,228
It's important to cultivate that kind of energy from a sense of achievement in your everyday life.

375
00:19:38,368 --> 00:19:41,288
I know it's true, but it's just so hard to do.

376
00:19:41,668 --> 00:19:47,008
Yeah, a sense of achievement and pain in the neck go hand in hand, but what can you do?

377
00:19:47,488 --> 00:19:52,468
I guess the best way to get that satisfaction is by overcoming the pain in the neck part.

378
00:19:58,468 --> 00:20:00,368
See you later! Thanks for dinner!

379
00:20:01,168 --> 00:20:05,928
I'll see you again soon! Here's to a great New Year!

380
00:20:11,368 --> 00:20:14,108
Oh no! I can't believe it's already this late!

381
00:20:14,628 --> 00:20:16,708
Hina, would you get Momo in the bath?

382
00:20:16,888 --> 00:20:17,328
Sure!

383
00:20:17,528 --> 00:20:18,848
Thanks, I'll handle the dishes.

384
00:20:20,208 --> 00:20:22,148
Rei, there's something I need to ask you.

385
00:20:22,648 --> 00:20:24,848
If you don't mind, we need to use this space.

386
00:20:25,728 --> 00:20:27,228
You're using this space?

387
00:20:27,888 --> 00:20:30,788
Yes. You've never seen it before, but...

388
00:20:30,788 --> 00:20:33,548
The Kawamoto House bath is...

389
00:20:33,548 --> 00:20:38,608
Right here.

390
00:20:40,048 --> 00:20:41,068
What the heck?

391
00:20:41,608 --> 00:20:41,968
Cheek!

392
00:20:41,968 --> 00:20:45,728
Long ago, we didn't have a bath, so we used a public one.

393
00:20:46,128 --> 00:20:50,648
But the family got bigger, so over the years, they decided to add on a bathroom.

394
00:20:51,388 --> 00:20:56,908
I know we're all girls here, but to be completely honest, it'd be really nice if we also had a changing room.

395
00:20:57,328 --> 00:21:01,348
If we did, though, it would take up the rest of the yard and cost a lot of money.

396
00:21:01,728 --> 00:21:05,108
But now, it's kind of embarrassing when we have guests.

397
00:21:05,108 --> 00:21:06,988
Thanks. Sorry about this, Rei.

398
00:21:07,188 --> 00:21:08,728
You're not supposed to look, Rei!

399
00:21:09,328 --> 00:21:11,708
Don't worry. Sorry for being in the way.

400
00:21:12,348 --> 00:21:14,088
Um, well, have a good night!

401
00:21:14,448 --> 00:21:15,508
Yeah, you too!

402
00:21:15,508 --> 00:21:20,848
That was... a total surprise!

403
00:21:21,228 --> 00:21:22,628
I've never seen that before!

404
00:21:23,128 --> 00:21:24,628
What an unusual house!

405
00:21:28,388 --> 00:21:29,348
Well...

406
00:21:29,348 --> 00:21:31,588
I took my medicine.

407
00:21:36,268 --> 00:21:38,348
This string is pretty convenient.

408
00:21:38,348 --> 00:21:46,028
It's kind of strange.

409
00:21:47,568 --> 00:21:50,628
Why am I spending nights here like it's a natural thing to do?

410
00:21:51,748 --> 00:21:54,408
I haven't even known this family for very long.

411
00:21:55,388 --> 00:21:57,728
Why do I feel so at peace when I'm here?

412
00:21:58,368 --> 00:22:00,868
Why does it feel... so right?

413
00:22:01,648 --> 00:22:04,848
I had... dreams of my childhood again.

414
00:22:07,188 --> 00:22:07,668
Why?

415
00:22:08,348 --> 00:22:09,888
Why do I feel so at peace when I'm here?

416
00:22:09,888 --> 00:22:11,328
Why do I feel so at peace?

417
00:22:11,328 --> 00:22:11,988
Why do I feel so at peace?

418
00:22:14,908 --> 00:22:15,608
Oh...

419
00:22:15,628 --> 00:22:16,408
Why do I feel so at peace when I'm here?

420
00:22:17,648 --> 00:22:18,488
I see.

421
00:22:22,488 --> 00:22:23,688
That's what it is.

422
00:22:26,108 --> 00:22:27,828
I had a feeling...

423
00:22:27,828 --> 00:22:30,208
I could tell...

424
00:22:30,208 --> 00:22:31,908
That this old house...

425
00:22:31,908 --> 00:22:33,108
Had time...

426
00:22:33,108 --> 00:22:33,928
And everything...

427
00:22:34,668 --> 00:22:36,068
And everyone...

428
00:22:36,068 --> 00:22:37,208
Even me...

429
00:22:37,208 --> 00:22:39,208
in a gentle embrace,

430
00:22:39,208 --> 00:22:42,208
and then it slowly faded away.

431
00:22:45,208 --> 00:22:47,208
With that in mind,

432
00:22:47,208 --> 00:22:49,208
I finally fell asleep.

433
00:22:49,208 --> 00:22:53,208
It was the kind of deep, peaceful sleep

434
00:22:53,208 --> 00:22:57,208
that I hadn't had in I don't know how many years.

435
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:35,411
Let's go get it, Kiriyama.

436
00:24:35,851 --> 00:24:37,051
I know this feeling.

437
00:24:38,531 --> 00:24:40,891
This is going to help us save so much money.

438
00:24:41,611 --> 00:24:44,191
Listen, Momo, you see?

439
00:24:45,411 --> 00:24:47,991
I have a match that I just can't lose.

440
00:24:48,811 --> 00:24:50,771
Rei, good luck.

441
00:24:51,011 --> 00:24:52,091
Oh, I'm so busy.

442
00:24:52,371 --> 00:24:53,971
I wish I had another pair of hands.

443
00:24:54,291 --> 00:24:55,011
Then I'll do it.

444
00:24:55,011 --> 00:24:58,151
Please watch the next episode of March Comes In Like a Lion.

445
00:25:01,011 --> 00:25:30,991
Thank you.

